# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated sample binaries
#
# These are built on demand by the scripts in examples/src/ and by the pytest
# fixtures. They are deliberately not committed: the generators are readable
# source, an opaque blob is not, and the evaluation ground truth in eval/suites
# is only auditable if the thing it describes can be regenerated from code.
#
# examples/vulnerable_demo.exe additionally contains deliberately unsafe calls
# and a fake AWS key, which is exactly the shape that makes endpoint scanners
# unhappy about a binary in a public repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
examples/*.elf
examples/*.exe
examples/*.bin
examples/*.so
examples/*.dll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aether project directories
#
# A project holds a SQLite database, a content-addressed blob store of every
# ingested file, and adapter scratch space. None of it belongs in git; use
# `aether export` for the Git-friendly representation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
aether.db
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
blobs/
work/
/work/
*.aether/

# Exported evidence graphs written at the repository root.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: a bare "export/" also matches the
# aether/export/ source package, which would silently drop a module from the
# repository.
/export/
/exports/

